                        "entry_id": "ed51b2ab-5c1d-35c8-a3e4-4c0a47e67986",
                        "glosses": [
                            "diakritisch teken in de vorm van twee puntjes dat geplaatst wordt op een klinker om aan te geven dat met deze letter een nieuwe lettergreep begint"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7b8ac452-197f-4a56-abe8-cabe5ed0b591",
                                "sense_id": "79aba1ca-b680-39c5-9b0a-b05eb5a818d0",
                                "text": "Het woord coëfficiënt heeft twee trema's."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7f371ba7-aba3-48a8-8efd-506f413f7d65",
                        "source_entry_id": "ed51b2ab-5c1d-35c8-a3e4-4c0a47e67986",
                        "source_sense_id": "79aba1ca-b680-39c5-9b0a-b05eb5a818d0",
                        "source_sense_description": "diakritisch teken",
                        "target_lang_word": "Trema",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Trema",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9294e66b-e485-3daa-8580-1465b9bb4bc7",
                                        "entry_id": "2ae5e07d-ac25-3f78-b529-12bc5ff40016",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Diakritikon/diakritisches Zeichen in der Schrift: waagerechter Doppelpunkt über Vokalen"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ee0ac8c4-851c-4ce0-be99-6df861d76e01",
                                                "sense_id": "9294e66b-e485-3daa-8580-1465b9bb4bc7",
                                                "text": "Das Trema hat im Deutschen und manchen anderen Sprachen zwei Funktionen:",
                                                "translation": "es zeigt an, dass eine Vokalfolge im Wort nicht als Diphthong, sondern als Folge von Vokalen zu sprechen ist (= Diärese); so z.B. in dem Namen des bedeutenden Phonetikers „Viëtor“."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6e22f636-5b56-4ec6-acef-2cad5c754d19",
                                                "sense_id": "9294e66b-e485-3daa-8580-1465b9bb4bc7",
                                                "text": "Im Russischen bezeichnet das Trema über einem „ë“ die Akzentstelle im Wort sowie Palatalisierung oder auch Jotierung."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d12f0da9-c0f9-4a21-a239-ddaea994b3d5",
                                                "sense_id": "9294e66b-e485-3daa-8580-1465b9bb4bc7",
                                                "text": "„Das Trema über einem Vokal bedeutet keinen Umlaut, sondern Dehnung (Ürümqi = Uuruumtschi).“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "40a205d9-9c4d-387a-a0a9-74e088f6debb",
                                        "entry_id": "2ae5e07d-ac25-3f78-b529-12bc5ff40016",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Diakritikon/diakritisches Zeichen in der Schrift: waagerechter Doppelpunkt über Vokalen",
                                            "diakritisches Zeichen zur Kennzeichnung einer getrennten Aussprache von Vokalen"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "im engeren Sinne"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5dba21aa-f1b3-4a1b-8107-8c682b355fa4",
                                                "sense_id": "40a205d9-9c4d-387a-a0a9-74e088f6debb",
                                                "text": "„Das Trema ist im heutigen Standarddeutsch eigentlich nicht gebräuchlich, jedoch kommt es bisweilen bei Eigennamen und Fremdwörtern vor.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c0d98630-a783-421c-9861-c84a292655b8",
                                                "sense_id": "40a205d9-9c4d-387a-a0a9-74e088f6debb",
                                                "text": "„Über das Trema. – Ä, Ö, Ü ſtatt Ae, Oe, Ue. […] Auch ſonſt wende man das Trema nur an, wo man glaubt, der unrichtigen Ausſprache des Geſchriebenen vorbeugen zu müſſen, z. B. etwa in Aï (Faultier), nicht aber bei Rhomboid, Atheiſt, Wörtern, die nicht leicht jemand falſch, d. h. zweiſilbig, ausſprechen wird.“ (spätes 19. Jahrhundert)"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1a\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "108918a7-fb33-36ac-89b3-0f73db206a16",
                                        "entry_id": "2ae5e07d-ac25-3f78-b529-12bc5ff40016",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Zahnlücke zwischen den vorderen Schneidezähnen, die nicht durch einen Zahnverlust bedingt ist"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Zahnmedizin"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "90b1fa5b-b287-4210-9e40-5fb91c975ecf",
                                                "sense_id": "108918a7-fb33-36ac-89b3-0f73db206a16",
                                                "text": "„Man unterscheidet das echte Diastema, das als Erbanomalie gilt, und das unechte Diastema. Dieses hat seine Ursache in der Nichtanlage oder in dem Verlust von einem oder zwei seitlichen Schneidezähnen.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5afebdc1-9d8e-40b6-81b0-5196e59f321d",
                        "source_entry_id": "ed51b2ab-5c1d-35c8-a3e4-4c0a47e67986",
                        "source_sense_id": "79aba1ca-b680-39c5-9b0a-b05eb5a818d0",
                        "source_sense_description": "diakritisch teken",
                        "target_lang_word": "diaeresis",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "diaeresis",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "96449637-1488-3d28-bdf2-3a90769a6229",
                                        "entry_id": "254bcfd4-fb13-3925-8aea-ca0af60c2d15",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A separation of one syllable (especially a vowel which is a diphthong, that is, beginning with one sound and ending with another) into two distinct syllables; distraction."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e03a167b-f122-4769-b54c-8c57664f8992",
                                                "sense_id": "96449637-1488-3d28-bdf2-3a90769a6229",
                                                "text": "Synaeresis, the opposite of Diaëresis, is the throwing of two syllables into one; as, Seest for seëst. Looked for look-ed."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "21b9423d-bf87-3b95-a509-865df1c58a2e",
                                        "entry_id": "254bcfd4-fb13-3925-8aea-ca0af60c2d15",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A separation of one syllable (especially a vowel which is a diphthong, that is, beginning with one sound and ending with another) into two distinct syllables; distraction.",
                                            "The diacritical mark consisting of two dots (¨) placed over a letter (especially the second of two consecutive vowels) to indicate that it is sounded separately, usually as a distinct syllable."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2242a405-ca4f-4e7c-8078-24d62defe9b7",
                                                "sense_id": "21b9423d-bf87-3b95-a509-865df1c58a2e",
                                                "text": "Diæreſis is vvhen tvvo points ouer a vovvell diuide it from another vovvel, as bouë, queuë, read bou-e, queu-e, not bo-ue, que-ue."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "93dfafbb-a3ed-40c2-be20-3ed54ef8f75b",
                                                "sense_id": "21b9423d-bf87-3b95-a509-865df1c58a2e",
                                                "text": "The Diæresis is used to divide a diphthong into two syllables; as, Creätor."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "38632019-2175-4350-b5f7-2782e51bcfc5",
                                                "sense_id": "21b9423d-bf87-3b95-a509-865df1c58a2e",
                                                "text": "An 85-year injustice has been rectified at Poets' Corner in Westminster Abbey with the corrected spelling of one of the greatest of all literary names. Reader, it is finally Brontë, not Bronte. An amended memorial to Charlotte, Emily and Anne Brontë was unveiled on Thursday with added diaereses (two dots) that ensure people pronounce it with two syllables. As if it rhymed with Monty, not font. The memorial was installed in 1939 and, for whatever reason, came without the diaereses that the Brontës used."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "57cb1611-2e39-3e12-9c25-11894705df24",
                                        "entry_id": "254bcfd4-fb13-3925-8aea-ca0af60c2d15",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An occurrence of separate vowel sounds in adjacent syllables without an intervening consonant; a hiatus."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1d8ae814-8c4f-339f-9b5e-b77da31bf6ff",
                                        "entry_id": "254bcfd4-fb13-3925-8aea-ca0af60c2d15",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A division, a separation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "rare",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "596116a9-c486-3ab4-9623-bd4ed1f059a6",
                                        "entry_id": "254bcfd4-fb13-3925-8aea-ca0af60c2d15",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A natural break in rhythm when a word ends at the end of a metrical foot in a line of verse."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d3f0a293-c2de-3b9c-968c-ddd95b15eced",
                                        "entry_id": "254bcfd4-fb13-3925-8aea-ca0af60c2d15",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An act of separating body parts or tissues which are normally together."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5623f884-0190-43e7-8fdb-aee7380b821f",
                                                "sense_id": "d3f0a293-c2de-3b9c-968c-ddd95b15eced",
                                                "text": "There are four^([sic]) manners of performing the Diæreſis: viz. by Cutting, Pricking, Tearing, Dravving, and Burning."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "804ad992-c8e7-4c36-81d9-8b7e6219b4c0",
